      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-255744",
      ":question/problem": "Given that we are considering only Boolean functions with $3$ variables $x_{1}$, $x_{2}$, and $x_{3}$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $x_{3}^(\u2015)$ is a literal\n2. $x_{2}\u2228x_{3}^(\u2015)$ is a maxterm\n3. $(x_{1}\u2228x_{2}\u2228x_{3})\u2227(x_{2}\u2228x_{3}^(\u2015))$ is a conjunctive normal form\n4. $(x_{1}\u2228x_{2}\u2228x_{3})\u2227(x_{2}\u2228x_{3}^(\u2015))$ is a principal conjunctive normal form"
