      ":question/problem": "Given that we are considering only Boolean functions with $3$ variables $x$, $y$, and $z$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $z^(\u2015)$ is a literal\n2. $x\u2228y\u2228z$ is a maxterm\n3. $(x^(\u2015)\u2228y\u2228z^(\u2015))\u2227(x\u2228y)$ is a conjunctive normal form\n4. $(x\u2228y^(\u2015)\u2228z)\u2227(x\u2228z)$ is a principal conjunctive normal form"
